  "CV200": {
    "code": "CV200",
    "name": "Mechanics of Solids",
    "branch": "CVE",
    "pdfPath": "/syllabi/CVE2025.pdf",
    "pdfName": "CVE2025.pdf",
    "ltp": "3-0-0",
    "credits": 3,
    "modules": [
      "Module 1 Stress & Strain: Introduction to material properties, Types of forces, Concept of\nstress & strain, Stress tensor & strain tensor, plane stress & Plane strain, differential equations\nof stress equilibrium, Saint Venant’s equation of compatibility, Stress-strain diagram of ductile\nand brittle material, Generalized Hooke’s law, Principle of superposition, compound and\ncomposite bars, thermal stresses and strain, statically determinate and indeterminate problems,\nStresses due to lack of fit or pre-strain, strain rosettes, Elastic Constant, Normal stress &\ntangential stress, Analytical & Graphical methods of stress analysis, Concept of principal\nstress, principal plane and its computation; Normal strain & tangential strain, Analytical &\nGraphical methods of strain analysis, Concept of Principal strains, principal strain in three\ndimensions, computation of principal stresses from the principal strains; Theory of Elastic\nfailure, Octahedral Shear stress theory, Superposition of yield surfaces; Concept of Strain\nEnergy, Elastic strain energy.",
      "Module 2 Shear Force & Bending Moment: Beams and support conditions, Types of supports\nand loads, shear force and bending moment, their diagrams for simply supported beams,\ncantilevers and overhanging beams.",
      "Module 3 Stresses in Beam (Bending & Shear Stresses): Theory of simple bending–Stress\ndistribution at a cross section due to Bending Moment and Shear Force, Curved bars,\nUnsymmetrical bending, Product moment of inertia, shear center.",
      "Module 4 Torsion: Torsion of circular elastic bars, torsion equation, introduction to warping\nof non-circular bars, power transmitted by shaft and hollow circular sections, Springs: Close\ncoiled helical spring subjected to axial load and axial torque.",
      "Module 5 Columns: Short and Long Column, stability of a long column, Euler’s Theory of\nColumns, differential equations of beam- columns, Derivation of Buckling Load for different\nend conditions, Rankine’s Formula.",
      "Module 6 Pressure Vessels: Thin and Thick cylinders subjected to internal pressures, Concept\nof stresses & strains, Hoop stress, Longitudinal stress in a cylinder, principal stresses in sphere\nand change in diameter and internal volume."
    ],
    "textbooks": [
      "1. Mechanics of Materials, Timoshenko and Gere, CBS Publishers, New Delhi, 2004, 2nd\nEdition.",
      "2. Mechanics of Materials, Beer and Johnston, McGraw Hill India Pvt. Ltd., 2020, 8th\nEdition (SI Units).",
      "3. Mechanics of Structures Vol 1 (Strength of Material), S. B. Junarkar and H. J. Shah,\nCharotar Publishing House Pvt. Ltd., 2012.\nReference books:",
      "1. Advanced Mechanics of Solids, L.S Srinath, McGraw Hill Education, 2017, 3rd\nEdition.",
      "2. Engineering Mechanics of Solids, E.P.Popov, Pearson, 2015, 2nd Edition.",
      "3. Strength of Materials - Fundamentals andApplications, T.D.Gunneswara Rao and\nMudimby Andal, Cambridge University Press, 2018, 1st Edition",
      "4. Strength of Materials - Pytel & Singer, Harper & Row Publishers, 2018, 4th Edition.\nOnline resources:",
      "1. https://nptel.ac.in/courses/105/105/105105108/"
    ],
    "objectives": [
      "1. Estimate solutions for elementary problems of mechanics of solids.",
      "2. Understand the behaviour of complex stresses on plane stress problems.",
      "3. Acquire all necessary fundamentals needed for pursuing courses on Structural Analysis\nand Structural Design.",
      "4. Understand the behaviour of beams under the action of bending & torsion.",
      "5. Develop the ability to check the stability of the columns & pressure vessels."
    ],
    "outcomes": [
      "At the end of the course, the student will be able to:"
    ]
  },
