  "CV203": {
    "code": "CV203",
    "name": "Engineering Geology",
    "branch": "CVE",
    "pdfPath": "/syllabi/CVE2025.pdf",
    "pdfName": "CVE2025.pdf",
    "ltp": "3-0-0",
    "credits": 3,
    "modules": [
      "Module 1: Introduction to Geology: Relevance of geology in Civil Engineering, Branches\nand scope of geology, Earth surface features and internal structure, rock weathering processes.",
      "Module 2: Mineralogy: Minerals, mineral classifications and identification based on\nphysical, optical, and chemical properties.",
      "Module 3: Petrology: Rock formation and their classification- igneous, sedimentary, and\nmetamorphic rocks, rock structures and textures. Exploration and testing of Rock, Rock\nQuality Designation (RQD), Borehole problems.",
      "Module 4: Structural geology: Geological Map, outcrop, attitude of beds, geological\nfeatures- folds, faults, unconformities, their types and classifications.",
      "Module 5: Hydrogeology: Ground water table, aquifers, subsurface distribution of\ngroundwater, groundwater in different geological formations, springs, geophysical\nexploration of groundwater.",
      "Module 6: Subsurface exploration methods: Soil profile, Fundamentals of Geophysical\nProspecting,- Seismic refraction method and electrical resistivity method.",
      "Module 7: Geohazards: Causes of earthquake and landslides, Remedial measures to mitigate\n\n\ndamage to engineering structures.",
      "Module 8: Dams and Tunnels: Types of dams, selection of dam sites, tunnels, geological\ninvestigation for a dam site, Seepage and leakage problems in dams- influencing factors and\nremedial measures. Geological consideration for tunneling, geothermal step, over break, stand\nup time, and logging of tunnels.\nList of Practicals:\n1. Identification of important minerals\n2. Classification and identification of Igneous, Sedimentary, and metamorphic rocks\n3. Structural geology- strike and dip, three and 3-point problems point problems.\n4. Structural geology – Completion of outcrops maps, order of superposition.\n5. Introduction to Geophysical methods for ground characterization-Electrical resistivity\nmethod, seismic refraction method"
    ],
    "textbooks": [
      "1. Text Book of Engineering Geology by N. Chenna Kesavulu, Mac Millan Ltd., New\nDelhi, 2018",
      "2. Engineering Geology, D Venkat Reddy, Viskas Publishing House Pvt. Ltd., 2017\nReference books:",
      "1. Engineering and General Geology – Parbin singh, Katson Publishers. 2013",
      "2. Principles of Engineering Geology – K.V.G.K. Gokhale, BS Publications,\nHyderabad, 2006.",
      "3. Engineering Geology – F.G. Bell, Elsevier Publications, 2007",
      "4. Principles of Engineering Geology and Geotechnics – D.P. Krynine, W.R. Judd,\n2018\nOnline Resources:",
      "1. https://nptel.ac.in/courses/105/105/105105106/"
    ],
    "objectives": [
      "1. Understand the dynamic nature of earth, the associated surface and subsurface processes\nand appreciate the importance of geology in civil engineering projects.",
      "2. Provide basic knowledge about different minerals, various rocks and their classification\nschemes and their engineering properties with their significance in civil engineering.",
      "3. Understand the process involved in rock deformation and formation of various geological\nstructures such as folds, faults, and joints unconformities.",
      "4. Understand the significance of various geological principles in planning, designing and\nconstruction of various civil projects and mitigation measures for natural hazards."
    ],
    "outcomes": [
      "At the end of the course, the student will be able to:"
    ]
  },
